  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 133 PM CST Thu Nov 12 2026\n\nThe current upper air analysis features a fairly amplified \npattern over the CONUS, with a deepening upper trough over the \nGreat Lakes region and upper ridging over the intermountain \nwest. This is resulting in a deep northerly flow regime across \nthe upper Midwest with some of the coldest air of the season \nadvecting swd across the region. \n\nAs is typically the case in these CAA regimes, sct/bkn stratocumulus \nclouds continue to advect swd across IA/IL.  Expect this to continue \ntomorrow into tomorrow night per the persistent cyclonic flow, with \npartly to mostly cloudy skies expected.  CAA will drop 850mb temps \nfrom -5C to -8C tonight and tomorrow. Although winds will not fully \ndecouple overnight, expect low temps tonight from the mid 20s north, \nto around 30F south.  Seasonally cold conditions will continue \ntomorrow, and nudged temps down a few degrees, preferring a blend of \nraw model temps. Highs will only reach the upper 30s north to the \nlower 40s south. Again, with very thin/limited moisture, expect dry \nconditions.",
